:trackLoadCapability rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                     rdfs:subPropertyOf :performanceObjParameter ;
                     rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                   owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                 :RunningTrack
                                               )
                                 ] ;
                     rdfs:range :LoadCapability ;
                     :XMLName "IPP_LoadCap" ;
                     :applicable "Y" ;
                     :formatNote """The value of this parameter is an instance of the era:LoadCapability class which consists of 2 properties:
- era:loadCapabilityLineCategory - as a taxonomy of load models representing line category
- era:loadCapabilitySpeed - integer for the value of speed [km/h] permitted for a specific load model

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, the data format is:
[CCCC] [NNN],
where:
- [CCCC] is a single selection from the predefined list of load models representing line category
- [NNN] is the value of speed [km/h] permitted for a specific load model."""@en ;
                     :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                     :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.2.4" ;
                     :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackLoadCapability> ;
                     :unitOfMeasure <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/KiloM-PER-HR> ;
                     :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                     <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2023-01-20"^^xsd:date ;
                     <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                         "2025-03-11"^^xsd:date ;
                     <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> :loadCapability ;
                     rdfs:comment "Relates the track with the class LoadCapability. A combination of the line category and speed at the weakest point of the track."@en ;
                     rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                     rdfs:label "Load capability"@en ;
                     rdfs:seeAlso """INF TSI: 4.2.1, 4.2.7.1, 4.2.7.2, 4.2.7.4
Annex D1 OPE TSI""" ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> """The set of selected data may include: B2-160, D4-120 and E5-100
When classifying infrastructure lines into line categories, the following options shall be used by the infrastructure manager to optimize freight traffic:
Option 1: determination of the line category at maximum freight traffic speed (maximum 120 Km/h)
Option 2: determination of a line category at an associated lower speed (less than the maximum freight traffic speed)
Example of option 1 (Annex F of EN 15528:2021): In a given track, if the traffic is mixed, the local speed of the line is 90 Km/h and the determined line category is D4 at a maximum of 90 Km/h, the information displayed should be: D4/90.
Example of option 2 (Annex F of EN 15528:2021): In a given track, if the traffic is mixed, the local speed of the line is 120 Km/h and the determined line category is C4 at a maximum of 120 Km/h and D4 at maximum of 90 Km/h, the information displayed should be: C4/120 and D4/90.""" ;
                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """At this step, RINF does not allow to enter additional data referred to additional speed regulations and operating requirements relating to locomotives (e.g., locomotive classes and associated maximum speed) or traffic types (e.g., maximum speed of freight traffic or passenger traffic).

The load capability describes the weakest point of this track within this section of line (which is normally a bridge or other sub-track structure).
It is expressed as a combination of the line category and speed permitted for trains exerting loads defined for this line category.
The result of the classification process is set out in EN 15528:2021 (Annex A) and referred to in that standard as Line Category.

The Load capability for UK in respect of Northern Ireland consists of RA and speed in miles per hour. RA shall be applied according to UK Railway Group Standard GE/RT8006, Issue Two, September 2010.

More than one combination may be published for the same track if applicable, but it has to be done by repetition of the parameter with one value selected only  that is why Y is given in line Can be repeated.
For the following cases, it is not possible to use EN 15528:2021 categories of line classification:
- TSI categories of line P1520 and F1520 (passenger traffic or freight traffic at any speed)
- TSI categories of line P1600 and F1600 (passenger traffic or freight traffic at any speed)

When more than one value of the parameter has to be published, then parameter has to be repeated as many times as many values of the parameter will be published."""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/trackObjParameter
:trackObjParameter rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                   rdfs:subPropertyOf :infraSubsystemObjParameter ;
                   :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.4" ,
                              "1.2.1.0.4" ;
                   <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                   rdfs:label "Track parameters"@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/trackPhaseInfo
:trackPhaseInfo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                rdfs:subPropertyOf :oclSeparationSectionsObjParameter ;
                rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                              owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                            :RunningTrack
                                          )
                            ] ;
                rdfs:range :PhaseInfo ;
                :XMLName "EOS_InfoPhase" ;
                :applicable "Y/N" ;
                :dependencyNote "A value is mandatory only if 1.1.1.2.4.1.1 parameter \"Phase separation\" value is \"Y\" (true), otherwise applicability flag is \"N\" (not applicable)"@en ;
                :formatNote """In RDF the range is an instance of the era:PhaseInfo class with all its properties.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, the data format is a character string with the following structure: distance type [MIN/MAX] + length [NNN] + switch off breaker [Y/N] + lower pantograph [Y/N] + km [NNN.NNN]. The structure of the string is as follows:
- distance type [MIN/MAX] - single selection of 'MIN=minimum' or 'MAX=maximum' to show whether the length is a minimum distance between the inner contact strips of the pantographs or a maximum distance between the outer contact strips of the pantographs. Multiple strings for this parameter are accepted;
- length [NNN] - the length of the phase separation in meters;
- switch off breaker [Y/N], single selection of 'yes' or 'no' to show whether the breaker has to be switched off;
- lower pantograph [Y/N], single selection of 'yes' or 'no' to show whether the pantograph has to be lowered,
- Km [NNN.NNN] - the location from the start of the line where the new value is valid."""@en ;
                :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.4.1.2" ;
                :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackPhaseInfo> ,
                                          <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackPhaseInfoApplicability> ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2023-04-05"^^xsd:date ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                    "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ,
                                                    "2025-06-09"^^xsd:date ;
                <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> :phaseInfo ;
                rdfs:comment "Relates the Track with PhaseInfo. Indication of required several information on phase separation."@en ;
                rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                rdfs:label "Information on phase separation"@en ;
                rdfs:seeAlso "ENE TSI: 4.2.15" ;
                <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/trackRaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed
:trackRaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf :pantographObjParameter ;
                                        rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                      owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                                    :RunningTrack
                                                                  )
                                                    ] ;
                                        rdfs:range :RaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed ;
                                        :XMLName "EPA_NumRaisedSpeed" ;
                                        :applicable "Y/N" ;
                                        :dependencyNote "Mandatory only if â€œOverhead contact line (OCL)â€ is selected in 1.1.1.2.2.1.1, otherwise the parameter is not applicable."@en ;
                                        :formatNote "Three values: [N] is number of pantographs; [NNN] is minimum distance between pantographs, in metres; [NNN] is the speed considered in km/h." ;
                                        :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                                        :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.3.3" ;
                                        :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackRaisedPantographDistanceAndSpeedApplicability> ,
                                                                  <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackRaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed> ;
                                        :usedInRCCCalculations "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2023-04-05"^^xsd:date ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2024-09-25"^^xsd:date ,
                                                                            "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/relation> :contactLineSystemType ;
                                        <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1301/2023-09-28> ,
                                                                          <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/1302/2023-09-28> ;
                                        rdfs:comment "Indication of maximum number of raised pantographs per train allowed and minimum spacing centre line to centre line of adjacent pantograph heads, expressed in metres, at the given speed."@en ;
                                        rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                                        rdfs:label "Requirements for number of raised pantographs and spacing between them, at the given speed"@en ;
                                        rdfs:seeAlso """ENE TSI: 4.2.13 ;
LOC&PAS TSI: 4.2.8.2.9.7""" ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "Relates the track with the class RaisedPantographsDistanceAndSpeed." ;
                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """This parameter gives the information about the number of pantographs and the distance between them at a given speed for which the Overhead Contact Line (OCL) has been designed.

As for different speeds different combinations of number of pantographs and distance between them may exist, so this parameter can be repeated to present all of them.

The raised pantographs distance and speed is the indication of maximum number of raised pantographs per train allowed and minimum spacing centre line to centre line of adjacent pantograph heads, expressed in metres, at the given speed.

See 4.2.13 (TSI ENE) and 4.2.8.2.9.7 (TSI LOC&PAS)"""@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/trackResistanceToAppliedLoadsObjParameter
:trackResistanceToAppliedLoadsObjParameter rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf :infraSubsystemObjParameter ;
                                           :rinfIndex "1.1.1.1.6" ;
                                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2024-10-31"^^xsd:date ;
                                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                                           rdfs:label "Track resistance to applied loads"@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/trackSystemSeparationInfo
:trackSystemSeparationInfo rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                           rdfs:subPropertyOf :oclSeparationSectionsObjParameter ;
                           rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                         owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                       :RunningTrack
                                                     )
                                       ] ;
                           rdfs:range :SystemSeparationInfo ;
                           :XMLName "EOS_InfoSystem" ;
                           :applicable "Y/N" ;
                           :dependencyNote "Mandatory if there is an indication of existence of system separation (parameter 1.1.1.2.4.2.1)"@en ;
                           :formatNote """In RDF, the range is an instance of the era:SystemSeparationInfo class with all its properties.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, the data format is a character string with the following structure: length [NNN] + switch off breaker [Y/N] + lower pantograph [Y/N] + km [NNN.NNN] """ ;
                           :legalDeadline "In accordance with Implementing Decision 2014/880/EU and by 16 March 2019 at the latest"@en ;
                           :rinfIndex "1.1.1.2.4.2.2" ;
                           :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackSystemSeparationInfo> ,
                                                     <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrackSystemSeparationInfoApplicability> ;
                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2023-04-05"^^xsd:date ;
                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2025-02-18"^^xsd:date ,
                                                               "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ,
                                                               "2025-06-09"^^xsd:date ;
                           <http://purl.org/dc/terms/replaces> :systemSeparationInfo ;
                           rdfs:comment "Indication of required several information on system separation"@en ;
                           rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                           rdfs:label "Information on system separation"@en ;
                           rdfs:seeAlso "ENE TSI: 4.2.16" ;
                           <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """Length - the length of the system separation in meters
Switch off breaker - single selection of  Y=yes  or  N=no  to show whether the breaker has to be switched off
Lower pantograph - single selection of  Y=yes  or  N=no  to show whether the pantograph has to be lowered
Km - the location from the start of the line where the new value is valid """@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/tracksideHabd
:tracksideHabd rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
               rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                             owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                           :RunningTrack
                                         )
                           ] ;
               rdfs:range :HABD ;
               <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2025-02-20"^^xsd:date ;
               rdfs:comment "Link between the running track and the HABD, covering the RINF parameters 1.1.1.1.7.(5-9)"@en ;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
               rdfs:label "hot axle box detector (HABD)"@en .


###  http://data.europa.eu/949/trainDetectionSystem
:trainDetectionSystem rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                      rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                    owl:unionOf ( :CommonCharacteristicsSubset
                                                  :RunningTrack
                                                )
                                  ] ;
                      rdfs:range :TrainDetectionSystem ;
                      :shaclShapeValidationRule <http://data.europa.eu/949/shapes/TrainDetectionSystem> ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2020-07-29"^^xsd:date ;
                      <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2021-09-12"^^xsd:date ,
                                                          "2025-02-28"^^xsd:date ;
                      rdfs:comment "Technical characteristics of the train detection systems installed in the section of line."@en ;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://data.europa.eu/949/> ;
                      rdfs:label "train detection system"@en ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2003/06/sw-vocab-status/ns#term_status> "stable" ;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> """It can be repeated as many times as the number of different train detection systems are present.
Not all parameters are applicable to all types of train detection systems; it depends on the applicability condition.
For RDF data provision:
The value of this property is an instance of the era:TrainDetectionsystem, which has as properties the parameters with indices 1.1.1.3.7.x.

For RINF XML data sets:
As long as the data provision through XML data sets is allowed, this property is the equivalent of the \"Set\" attribute, grouping parameters 1.1.1.3.7.x."""@en .


